      "message": "Since these variable are only used inside the mutex, they should not be declared here.\n\nNote that as opposed to C, in C++ you may declare variable not at the beginning of the function. In fact, you should do that, because their declaration also calls the constructor, which is something you don\u0027t always want to do, like in the case the server is already running and doesn\u0027t have to be created, you don\u0027t need the construcor of `grpc::ServerBuilder` to be called. Another example is `server_creds`, which you construct here and never used the constructed object until you copy a value to it in line 104, which is an anti-pattern in C++.",
